    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97c76e81_b15e9990",
        "filename": "tests/scan_utils_unittest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-11T02:00:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ACTION_P is hard to think about, since it\u0027s a macro. Between the implicit symbols (arg0, arg1), and the lack of types, it\u0027s hard to understand what\u0027s going on.\n\n(I appreciate the comment you provided, to help sort that out. But it\u0027s even better if the code doesn\u0027t need comments. :-))\n\nConsider using a function template like the following, instead:\n\n    template \u003cint ControlMessageErrorCode, bool ReturnValue\u003e\n    bool AppendControlMessageAndReturn(\n        const NL80211Packet\u0026 /* request message */,\n        std::vector\u003cstd::unique_ptr\u003cconst NL80211Packet\u003e\u003e* reply) {\n      reply-\u003epush_back(std::make_unique\u003cNL80211Packet\u003e(\n          CreateControlMessageError(ControlMessageErrorCode)));\n      return ReturnValue;\n}\n\n(Note that you\u0027ll need to remove -std\u003dc++11 from Android.mk, to allow use of make_unique. But I believe that c++14 is now the default. And unless there\u0027s a specific reason for specifying a lower version, we shouldn\u0027t.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "bab4da8b037ff1cbda7b977116f530aed12639f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a364350b_0ef614a9",
        "filename": "tests/scan_utils_unittest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-11T23:31:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes ACTION_P is hard to read and to use.\nYour sample code is great if we only need to append a control message.\nHowever we might need to append more complex messages in later work. E.g. Mock the responses of GetScanResult(), which are complex NL80211 packets.\nIn those cases, if we use non-type template parameters like the following:\n\ntemplate \u003cvector\u003cNL80211Packet\u003e, bool ReturnValue\u003e\n    bool AppendMessageAndReturn() {\n  ...\n}\n\nThen compiler is not happy with that because vector\u003cNL80211Packet\u003e can not be inferred.\nWith that said, instead I use additional arguments instead of template parameters here.\nIn test cases these additional arguments will be pre-bounded by std::bind().",
      "parentUuid": "97c76e81_b15e9990",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "bab4da8b037ff1cbda7b977116f530aed12639f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
